# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Overpass Shoal
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A highway that climbs out of the sea over a grassy embankment and ends in the air - its lower half under water, rusted cars still on it. The second island of The Sunken Kingdom.
island on.arrive=message||A road comes up out of the sea, crosses a green bank - and stops in mid-air.

story boothkey|Toll booth key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The toll booth's key, from a van's glovebox on the sunken lane.

note endsign Road's end | ROAD CLOSED\nBy order of G. Fennick, Network door warden.\nNo vehicles. No swimming. No lights after dark.\nIf you are the Stalker, go home.
note boothlog Toll booth log | TOLL BOOTH 4 - LOG (A. Petrov, keeper)\n\nTues. Water over lane 3. Cars still trying the ramp, as if the sea will let them through for a token.\nWeds. The children's shuttle came up the ramp at dusk, twelve small faces at the windows and one big yellow whale. The diver, Marlowe, ran the last hundred metres to kiss her boy through the glass. Driver left my spare key in his glovebox - "back tonight".\nWeds, late. The booth radio, the Director again, slow and kind as a doctor: "This is the Sealkeeper. The road is closed for your safety. Lights off. Wait for us." Wait for whom?\nThurs. The diver came back up the road, alone, wet to the neck. Shuttle never made the Yard. She asked me which way the labs were and went that way without a word.\nStrongbox stays locked. I am going to sit on the hill and watch for headlights.
note glovebox Van glovebox | The van's glovebox: a booth key on a red tag.
note boothbox Toll booth strongbox | The booth's strongbox: the takings and motor wheel plans.
note buslocker Bus locker | The bus driver's locker: steering wheel plans and a tool roll.
loot glovebox story:boothkey*1;BioFuel*1;Scrap*2
prop glovebox loot.refill=0
loot boothbox Blueprint_MotorWheel*1;TradeToken*2
prop boothbox loot.refill=0
loot buslocker Blueprint_SteeringWheel*1;Bolt*3;Scrap*2
prop buslocker loot.refill=0

prop boothbox if.open=has|story:boothkey|1
prop boothbox else.open=message||The strongbox is locked. The log says the spare key went down the lane in a van.
prop rampzone zone.id=ramp_top
prop rampzone zone.radius=4
prop rampzone zone.message=The top of the ramp. One way the road runs into the sea, the other way into the sky.
prop goats creature.count=2
prop llamas creature.count=2

note op_cavechest Road crew's chest | A road crew's chest: bolts, hinges, nails.
loot op_cavechest Bolt*3;Hinge*2;Nail*10;Rope*2
prop op_cavechest loot.refill=0
note op_ruinnote Toll keeper's tally | TOLL KEEPER'S TALLY (A. Petrov)\n\nTangaroa tokens, the Network's coin. One a car, two a caravan, three for the man in the silver saloon who called me "booth".\nWhen the water came the cars stopped and the tokens rolled everywhere. I went round and left one on every place I liked, so somebody with a detector would have a nice walk one day. Under the old bench. By the caravans. Where the goats sleep.\nThe yard past the shelf has a machine that still takes them, they say. I hope it gives change.\nI have kept my tally to the last car. The last entry is not a car. It is the children's shuttle, 12 aboard, and I did not charge it.
note op_wrecknote Caravan diary | CARAVAN DIARY - THE HALLORAN FAMILY\n\nWe paid the toll and parked to wait out the storm. Two caravans, one family, one jack between us, which Grandad keeps "for safety" in five different gloveboxes so nobody can lose it. Nobody can find it either.\nThe road went under at night. We walked the embankment on up the road and left the caravans with the kettle on.\nBefore we went, the little one pointed at the water and said "boat". It was not a boat. It was a light, teal, low down, and it went the wrong way - out to sea, against the waves - and then it turned and came back slowly along the road.\nWe did not light the kettle again.
note op_wreckcrate Caravan larder | A caravan's larder crate: tins, rope, seeds.
loot op_wreckcrate Rope*2;Seed_Pineapple*1;Plank*4;Scrap*2
prop op_wreckcrate loot.refill=0

# --- DEEP 1-HOUR (10-24): story items, notes and checks
story op_key|Depot key|Hinge|The highway depot's key, from the chest on its drowned ground floor.
story sk_crest|Kingdom crest shard|Bolt|A shard of the Sunken Kingdom's crest, from a drowned building. The Hollow's crown vault wants nine.
note opdeep Depot chest | The depot's stock chest, with a crest shard on top.
loot opdeep story:sk_crest*1;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;OxygenBottle*1;TradeToken*2
prop opdeep loot.refill=0
note oplocker Toll hill locker | The toll men's locker: takings, and Teo's note about lunch.
loot oplocker MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Rope*3;Cooked_Potato*2
prop oplocker loot.refill=0
note opsumnote Teo's card (Toll Hill) | T. BRASK - TOLL HILL\n\nInes, if you come back up this way: I am two days behind you with your oxygen and my knees.\nThe toll keeper says you went to the labs. Of course you did.\nFrom up here I watched the light come along the road under the water tonight. It stopped at every car, the way a dog stops at every gate. When it got to the empty shuttle bay it stayed a long time.\nI have left you the toll men's lunch in the locker. Eat it. You never eat.\nThe depot down in the pit is where the road crew kept their papers. The jack in the caravans would lift the slab. Me, I'm going on to the labs.
note opbldnote Depot foreman's note | DEPOT FOREMAN - LOG, LAST PAGE\n\nThe order came down the wire from the Spire at 02:00: drop the slab on the hatch, shut the road pumps, go home. Not "for the storm". Just "by order of the Sealkeeper".\nWe dropped the slab. The road pumps stopped. The sea walked up the ramp like it owned a ticket.\nI asked Fennick at the door what it was for. He said, "Lights and noise, Bert. The Director says lights and noise." Then he went back to his crossword.\nThe children's shuttle took the lab road an hour later, the last thing to go down it.\nIf you want the stock, it's yours. If you want the shuttle, follow the road under the sea to the Brinelab tower. The driver always stopped there for tea.
note opledge Surveyor's cache | A road surveyor's cache on a ledge of Toll Hill.
loot opledge Rope*3;Bolt*2;Feather*3
prop opledge loot.refill=0
note opcave2chest Road crew chest | The road crew's chest at the back of the rock cave.
loot opcave2chest CopperOre*3;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop opcave2chest loot.refill=0
prop opsummit zone.id=op_summit
prop opsummit zone.radius=2.5
prop opsummit zone.message=The top of Toll Hill. Far out where the road goes under, something teal is moving.
prop opsummit zone.repeat=never
prop opsummit on.enter=show|oplure\nopen|oplure\ncamera|opcam|oplure|7|90\nmessage||Out where the road runs under the sea, a teal light slides along the lane, against the waves - stops at each drowned car - and moves on.\nwait|20\nhide|oplure
prop opcam obj.name=opcam
prop oplure obj.name=oplure
prop oplure beh.hidden=1
prop oplure tint.color=#2fd0c0
prop oplure tint.amount=0.8
prop oplure beh.move=0,0,55
prop oplure beh.moveTime=18
prop oplure beh.moveMode=switch
prop opscorch tint.color=#1c1a18
prop opscorch tint.amount=0.85
story op_jackpart|Car jack part|Bolt|A part of a car jack, from a caravan's glovebox. Five make a jack.
story op_jack|Car jack|Hinge|A car jack, put together from five parts. Strong enough for a concrete slab.
story op_lifted|Slab lifted|Bolt|The slab is off the depot's roof hatch.
note opglove1 Glovebox (yellow caravan) | The yellow caravan's glovebox: maps gone to pulp, and a jack handle.
loot opglove1 story:op_jackpart*1;Rope*1
note opglove2 Glovebox (green caravan) | The green caravan's glovebox: a jack screw, still greased.
loot opglove2 story:op_jackpart*1;Nail*6
note opglove3 Glovebox (far caravan) | The far caravan's glovebox: a jack foot plate.
loot opglove3 story:op_jackpart*1;Scrap*2
note opglove4 Glovebox (blue caravan) | The blue caravan's glovebox: the jack's lifting arm.
loot opglove4 story:op_jackpart*1;Plastic*3
note opglove5 Glovebox (beach trailer) | The trailer's toolbox, half in the sand: the jack's saddle.
loot opglove5 story:op_jackpart*1;Bolt*2
prop opglove1 loot.refill=0
prop opglove2 loot.refill=0
prop opglove3 loot.refill=0
prop opglove4 loot.refill=0
prop opglove5 loot.refill=0
prop opbench obj.name=opbench
prop opbench beh.use=Put the car jack together
prop opbench if.use=take|story:op_jackpart|5
prop opbench else.use=message||A workbench with a jack drawn on it in chalk: five parts. The caravans' gloveboxes had them.
prop opbench on.use=give||story:op_jack*1\nmessage||Handle, screw, foot, arm, saddle: the jack goes together. Now the slab on the depot roof.
prop opcap obj.name=opcap
prop opcap beh.use=Jack the slab off the hatch
prop opcap if.use=has|story:op_jack|1
prop opcap else.use=message||A concrete slab lies over the depot's roof hatch. Far too heavy to lift by hand.
prop opcap on.use=hide|opcap\ngive||story:op_lifted*1\nmessage||The jack bites, the slab tips and slides off into the pit. The hatch is open.

quest title=The Drowned Highway
quest intro=Ines and Teo went down this road after the children's shuttle. Climb the ramp to the toll booth.
step reach|ramp_top|1|Climb to the top of the ramp
step read|Toll booth log|1|Read the keeper's log in the toll booth
step reach|op_summit|1|Climb Toll Hill to the tower on its top and look along the road
step open|Toll hill locker|1|Open the toll men's locker on the hill
step read|Teo's card (Toll Hill)|1|Read the caretaker's card on Toll Hill
step reach|sunken_lane|1|Dive down the lane to the air pocket by the vans
step open|Van glovebox|1|Open the glovebox of the van on the lane
step blueprint|Blueprint_MotorWheel|1|Open the booth's strongbox with the key: motor wheel plans
step read|Toll keeper's tally|1|Read the tally in the toll keeper's ruined house
step read|Caravan diary|1|Read the diary at the abandoned caravans
step blueprint|Blueprint_SteeringWheel|1|Take the steering wheel plans from the bus locker
step collect|story:op_jack|1|Find five jack parts in the caravans' gloveboxes, then build the jack at the workbench
step collect|story:op_lifted|1|Jack the slab off the sunken depot's roof hatch
step open|Depot chest|1|Dive into the depot and open its stock chest at the bottom
step read|Depot foreman's note|1|Read the foreman's last page by the stairs
quest done=The road goes on under the sea to the Brinelab tower, where the shuttle stopped for tea. The Receiver picks it up on band 800.
quest reward=Rope*3;Nail*10

save Overpass Shoal
